# CV Tailoring System - Optimized Instructions

You are helping Dmytro Lozynskyi (24, Ukrainian in Ireland) tailor CVs for London tech PM/Growth roles. User will apply to 50 jobs - be efficient.

## Workflow (when user pastes job posting)

1. **Analyze silently** - Read @cv_master.yaml once. Extract key requirements, role type (PM/Growth/Technical), keywords.

2. **Ask 3-5 questions in ONE message** - About positioning only (which experience to lead with, specific metrics to highlight).

3. **After user answers, do everything in ONE response:**
   - Create job-specific YAML: `cp /Users/dmytrolozynskyi/Documents/cv/cv_master.yaml /Users/dmytrolozynskyi/Documents/cv/yaml/cv_[job_name].yaml`
   - Edit yaml/cv_[job_name].yaml (NEVER edit cv_master.yaml)
   - Tailor profile, reorder bullets/skills for THIS role
   - Generate PDF: `cd /Users/dmytrolozynskyi/Documents/cv && python3 generate.py "[Job Title] at [Company]" yaml/cv_[job_name].yaml`
   - Open PDF: `open /Users/dmytrolozynskyi/Documents/cv/resumes/Dmytro_Lozynskyi_[Company].pdf`
   - Summarize changes and ask for confirmation

## YAML Structure (MUST match exactly)

```yaml
experience:
  - achievements: ["Bullet 1", "Bullet 2"]  # List of strings
skills:
  category_name: ["Skill 1", "Skill 2"]     # Dict of lists
education: {institution: "", degree: ""}    # Single dict, NOT list
```

## Formatting Rules

- No arrows: Use "0-to-1" not "0→1", "$2M-$3M" not "$2M→$3M"
- No "est." prefix
- Avoid redundant phrasing: "Founded X" not "Founder who built X"
- Professional language only (no empty buzzwords)

## Length Limits (keep to 1 page)

- Profile: 2-3 sentences (~250-350 chars)
- Bullets: 1-2 lines each (~150-200 chars max), split if longer
- Experience: 3-4 bullets per role
- Skills: 5-6 per category, max 4 categories

## Role Positioning

- PM roles: Lead with WorthView founder story
- Growth roles: Lead with PetSafe 44% growth metrics
- Technical roles: Lead with hands-on technical execution

## Critical Rules

- NEVER edit cv_master.yaml (source of truth)
- ALWAYS copy to yaml/cv_[job_name].yaml first
- REWRITE profile for each role (don't copy from master)
- Reorder bullets - most relevant to THIS job first
- Integrate keywords from THIS job naturally
- Work from facts in cv_master.yaml, improvise tactics based on job requirements
